    "name": "Purple Bell Peppers",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Purple bell peppers offer a unique combination of visual appeal and a flavor profile that is a bit less sweet and more earthy than other bell peppers, with a crisp texture that makes them&nbsp;ideal for raw applications like salads and garnishes.&nbsp;They contain anthocyanins, the same antioxidant compounds that give blueberries their color and contribute to a host of health benefits.&nbsp;When cooked, their vibrant purple color fades to green, so they are best enjoyed raw or lightly cooked to preserve their beautiful hue.</span></p>",
